IN SHORT (this summary is part of the license; sections 1 to 11 give the
detail):

- This code is public ONLY so that anyone can check what the SpendBranch CLI
  does before installing it on their machine. Being able to see it does not
  mean you may use it.
- It is NOT open source. It is proprietary software that you may read.
- You may NOT copy it, reuse it, fork it, or take any part of it (code,
  structure, design or logic) into another project, whether yours or anyone
  else's, commercial or not.
- You may NOT use it to train, fine-tune, evaluate or improve any artificial
  intelligence or machine learning model, or put it in any dataset.

1. DEFINITIONS

"Software" means everything in this repository: source code, schemas, test
fixtures, test vectors, build and CI configuration, and documentation, and
any part, excerpt or translation of it.

"SpendBranch" means the owner of this repository and its authorized
representatives.

"Official Binary" means an executable built and distributed by SpendBranch
through the channels SpendBranch designates for that purpose.

"Audit Purpose" means inspecting, verifying, testing or researching the
Software in order to understand what it does, to assess its security and
privacy properties, or to confirm that an Official Binary corresponds to this
source code.

"AI System" means any artificial intelligence or machine learning model or
system, including large language models, code generation models and code
assistants, and any dataset, corpus, index or embedding store used to build,
train, tune, evaluate or feed one.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

You may, free of charge and for an Audit Purpose only:

a. view, read, search and analyze the Software, including with automated
   analysis tools (such as linters, scanners, debuggers, or an AI assistant
   you direct to review it), subject to section 4;
b. download an unmodified copy of the Software, build it unmodified on your own
   machines, and run its tests and the resulting build, solely to carry out the
   audit (including comparing the result with an Official Binary);
c. quote short excerpts of the Software, with attribution, in security
   reports, research, reviews and technical discussion about the Software;
d. report issues, vulnerabilities and suggestions to SpendBranch.

Nothing else is permitted. If a use is not listed in this section, it is not
allowed.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

Except as SpendBranch expressly permits in writing, you may not:

a. use the Software, or anything derived from it, for any commercial purpose,
   or in any product, service or project, whether or not you charge for it;
b. fork the Software, or create any derivative work from it;
c. copy, reuse or reimplement the Software, in whole or in part, in any other
   software, including by copying, retyping, translating it into another
   programming language, or closely reproducing its code, structure, sequence,
   organization, protocols or logic;
d. modify, adapt, port or patch the Software, other than the temporary, local,
   unredistributed changes strictly needed to run an audit (for example,
   adding logging to observe behavior), which you must discard when the audit
   ends;
e. copy, publish, host, mirror, distribute, sublicense, sell, lease or
   otherwise make the Software available to anyone else, in source or binary
   form, in whole or in part (other than the excerpts allowed in section 2c);
f. run or deploy a build you made yourself as a substitute for an Official
   Binary, or offer one to others;
g. remove or alter any copyright, license or attribution notice;
h. use the SpendBranch name, logos or marks to endorse or promote anything
   without permission.

Using an Official Binary is governed by the terms under which SpendBranch
provides it, not by this license.

4. ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE AND MACHINE LEARNING

The Software may not be used by, for, or to build any AI System. In
particular, you may not, and you may not allow or help anyone else to:

a. use the Software, in whole or in part, to train, pre-train, fine-tune,
   distill, align, evaluate or benchmark any AI System, or to otherwise
   improve one;
b. include the Software in any dataset, corpus, archive, index or embedding
   store that is, or may be, used for any purpose listed in 4a;
c. scrape, crawl, download or collect the Software for any purpose listed in
   4a or 4b;
d. use the Software as retrieval or reference material from which an AI
   System generates code or content for anyone other than an auditor carrying
   out an Audit Purpose.

Using an AI assistant to help you audit the Software, as allowed in section
2a, is permitted only if the provider of that assistant does not keep the
Software or use it for any purpose listed in 4a or 4b.

This section applies to everyone, including operators of AI Systems and of
the crawlers and services that collect data for them, and it applies whether
the Software was obtained from this repository, from a fork, mirror, cache or
archive, or from any other source.

